Two of the operations requests are not included. The node has no filesystem capability, since `wasm32-unknown-unknown` has no WASI and the world imports nothing for file access. The metadata fetch would need an `http-client` import, which this node is not granted, and it would send digest text to an external service. Both change what the node can reach, so they need an explicit capability grant from the graph owner. The node below does only what its contract requires: it notifies the digest and reports whether the notification was accepted.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{digest, published-digest};

    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;

    export run: func(composed: digest) -> published-digest;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(composed: Digest) -> PublishedDigest {
        let mut message = format!("Digest {}\n{}", composed.date, composed.overview);
        for entry in composed.entries.iter().filter(|e| e.kept) {
            message.push_str("\n- ");
            message.push_str(&entry.title);
            message.push_str(" (");
            message.push_str(&entry.link);
            message.push(')');
        }

        let published = crate::aap::caps::notifier::notify(&message);

        PublishedDigest {
            date: composed.date,
            considered: composed.considered,
            published,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
